      {
        "id": "f3f465c9-d82c-4be0-8e16-cb47e20ac2b8",
        "name": "Notes",
        "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
        "typeVersion": 1,
        "position": [
          0,
          -80
        ],
        "parameters": {
          "color": 4,
          "width": 1500,
          "height": 220,
          "content": "## Approved PR Merger (C8 #35, C9 #37)\n\n**Human-approved PRs (not Dependabot):** Brian's approval is the merge trigger. Search `review:approved` (sweep) or the ingress calls this on a `pull_request_review` approved event. Merge only when `mergeable_state == clean`; squash as oneshot-pr-bot with the head SHA pinned.\n\n**Dependabot PRs (policy, Brian 2026-09-20):** pre-approved, no human. Search `author:app/dependabot`. Open, not draft, mergeable, state blocked/clean/unstable -> fetch check runs and the base branch's required status contexts. Green means: every required context has a successful run; if the branch has no required contexts, at least one run exists and all are successful. Non-required jobs (old preview deploy / flag-major) do not block. Then the bot submits the APPROVE review itself (it is not the author, so protection accepts it) and squash-merges. A repo with no checks at all never auto-merges: nothing was tested.\n\nNo model call anywhere here. Failed API calls are error executions. Runs every 5 min plus on every approval event."
        }
      },
